# F1 / S2 — class-identity corpus driver for the PURE-SIMPLE FRONTEND
# INTERPRETER.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# The F1 corpus (spec + probe) can only reach the Rust SEED:
#   bin/simple run <file>                 -> seed JIT (cranelift)
#   SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpret ...   -> seed tree-walk
# Neither touches src/compiler/10.frontend/core/interpreter/**, which is the
# engine lane F1's step S1 modifies. Measuring S1 therefore needs a driver that
# calls the pure-Simple frontend interpreter DIRECTLY. That is this file.
#
# HOW IT REACHES THE OTHER ENGINE
# -------------------------------
# `core_jit_interpret(source, path, threshold)`
# (10.frontend/core/interpreter/mod.spl:248) runs the pure-Simple pipeline
# lex -> parse -> eval_module over `source`. With threshold 999999 the JIT never
# fires, so every case is decided by the pure-Simple TREE-WALK evaluator
# (eval_stmts.spl / eval_calls.spl / _EvalOps), not by the seed. The seed still
# executes THIS file -- it is the host -- but it does not decide the corpus
# answers.
#
# HOW YOU KNOW IT IS NOT SILENTLY THE SEED (positive discriminator)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Case A (class in a trait-typed field) is REF here and COPY(n=100) under
# `SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpret bin/simple run` on the same file. Case B is
# answered here but KILLS the seed JIT process. A fallback to either seed engine
# is therefore visible in the output, not silent. Run
# `scripts/check/check-class-identity-engine-matrix.shs` to print all three
# lanes side by side and assert the divergence.
#
# The `use` block below is exhaustive on purpose: the interpreter package's
# `__init__.spl` exports a hand-maintained SUBSET of its own symbols (see the
# comment there about `eval_int_method`), so a driver that imports only the
# barrel dies with E1002 on the first unexported internal. Importing every
# module by path is what makes an out-of-tree driver viable at all.
#
# RUN IT FROM OUTSIDE THE REPO TREE (defect workaround, measured 2026-08-09).
# Byte-identical file, same env, same binary:
#   bin/simple run scripts/check/class_identity_pure_simple_driver.spl
#     -> error: semantic: variable `cache_initialized` not found
#        (a module-level `var` in 10.frontend/core/interpreter/value.spl -- the
#         imported package's own globals were never initialised)
#   cp to /tmp and `bin/simple run /tmp/<copy>.spl` from the repo root
#     -> runs to completion, all ten cases answered
# The entry file's LOCATION decides whether imported modules' globals get
# initialised. `scripts/check/check-class-identity-engine-matrix.shs` does the
# copy for you; keep the working directory at the repo root either way, because
# the case paths below are relative to it.
#
# Usage:
#   sh scripts/check/check-class-identity-engine-matrix.shs      # preferred
#   cp scripts/check/class_identity_pure_simple_driver.spl /tmp/d.spl && \
#     SIMPLE_MODULE_LIMIT=4000 bin/simple run /tmp/d.spl
# Each case runs as an INDEPENDENT eval, so a failure in one case cannot hide
# the ones after it (the single-file probe stops at the first error).

